Level-Up Project: Smart Hospital Management System
Scenario

A hospital wants software to manage doctors, patients, appointments, billing, and medical records.

Design the system using proper OOP principles.

Requirements
1. Abstraction

Create an abstract class:

Person

Abstract methods

login()
display_profile()

Doctor and Patient must implement these methods.

2. Inheritance
Person
     |
---------------------
|                   |
Doctor          Patient

Both inherit common data.

3. Polymorphism

Create

show_dashboard(person)

When passed

Doctor

it shows doctor's dashboard.

When passed

Patient

it shows patient's dashboard.

Same function.

Different behavior.

4. Composition

Every patient has

MedicalRecord

If Patient is deleted

↓

MedicalRecord is also deleted.

Example

Patient
   |
MedicalRecord

MedicalRecord cannot exist without Patient.

5. Aggregation

Hospital stores doctors.

Doctor can leave Hospital.

Hospital deleted?

Doctor still exists.

Hospital -----> Doctor
6. Association

Doctor treats Patient.

Neither owns the other.

Doctor <-------> Patient

Doctor can treat many patients.

Patient can visit many doctors.

7. Encapsulation

Keep

medical history
salary
password

private.

Use

__variable
8. Property Decorator

Patient

age

cannot become

-5

Use

@property
@age.setter

Validate.

Doctor

experience

Cannot be negative.

Again use property.

9. Decorator

Create your own decorator

@log_activity

Whenever these methods run

book_appointment()

cancel_appointment()

generate_bill()

Decorator prints

[LOG]
Method Name
Current Time
Finished Successfully

No logging code inside these methods.

10. Bill

Create

Bill

Use property

amount

Cannot be negative.

11. Extra Polymorphism

Create

Payment

Method

pay()

Implement

CashPayment

CardPayment

UPIPayment

Hospital simply calls

payment.pay()

without checking payment type.

12. Appointment

Each appointment contains

Doctor

Patient

Date

Time

Hospital stores all appointments.

13. Bonus Challenge (Optional)

Implement a singleton-like class (or another suitable design) so that only one Hospital object should exist in the program.

Constraints
❌ No global variables.
❌ No copy-paste code between Doctor and Patient.
❌ No direct access to private variables from outside the class.
❌ Don't use dictionaries for everything—model the system with classes.
✅ Use meaningful methods.
✅ Follow good OOP design.